      "category": "precipitate strengthening",
      "sample_id": "sample_1",
      "material_state": "aged",
      "assertion_level": "author_interpretation",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 6,
          "section": "4.1. The γ′ precipitate strengthening at room temperature",
          "quote": "Based on calculated results in Fig. S-6, the precipitates strengthening mechanism in the primary γ′ phase is strong pair-coupling precipitate shearing while the secondary γ′ phase is weak pair-coupling precipitate shearing.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": "S-6",
          "chunk_id": "d8b2611a299602d2:part:002"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "mechanism_2",
      "name": "coherency stress",
      "category": "precipitate strengthening",
      "sample_id": "sample_2",
      "material_state": "aged",
      "assertion_level": "author_interpretation",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 7,
          "section": "4.2. The γ′ precipitate strengthening at high temperature",
          "quote": "According to a simplified model for coherency stress calculation [47], the coherency stress contribution can be expressed by Δσcoherent = Vγ′ δ E[100], where E[100] should be the elastic modulus of the γ matrix. By calculation, the coherency stresses in Coalloy-2Ta are 274 MPa at 900 ◦C, which is 55% of the yield stress of Coalloy-2Ta at 900 ◦C, i.e. 495 MPa.",
          "table": "5",
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "d8b2611a299602d2:part:002"
        }
      ]
    }
